+// Defined in core/device.cu. Records what the host is about to enqueue so that a sticky CUDA error
+// can name it instead of naming the unrelated call that first synchronises. It is a host pointer
+// store, so it changes no GPU ordering and cannot mask the defect it is meant to observe.
+// The declaration is deliberately at file scope: written inside the execution namespace below it
